    "q-147971": {
      "dom_id": "step-q147971",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.65$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0+1.2 \\\\  & =1.2 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.65+3\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =0.65+1.05 \\\\  & =1.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.2)(y-1.7)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0-1.2)(1-1.7)f(0,1) \\\\  & +(0-1.2)(3-1.7)f(0,3) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(1-1.7)f(2,1) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(3-1.7)f(2,3) \\\\  & =(-1.2)(-0.7)(0.15) \\\\  & +(-1.2)(1.3)(0.25) \\\\  & +(0.8)(-0.7)(0.5) \\\\  & +(0.8)(1.3)(0.1) \\\\  & =-0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
