    "q-147970": {
      "dom_id": "step-q147970",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.8+1.8 \\\\  & =2.6 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.7+2\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0.7+0.6 \\\\  & =1.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2.6)(y-1.3)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(2-2.6)(1-1.3)f(2,1) \\\\  & +(2-2.6)(2-1.3)f(2,2) \\\\  & +(3-2.6)(1-1.3)f(3,1) \\\\  & +(3-2.6)(2-1.3)f(3,2) \\\\  & =(-0.6)(-0.3)(0.3) \\\\  & +(-0.6)(0.7)(0.1) \\\\  & +(0.4)(-0.3)(0.4) \\\\  & +(0.4)(0.7)(0.2) \\\\  & =0.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
