    "q-147967": {
      "dom_id": "step-q147967",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.5$ | $0$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+3\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5+1.5 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.7+4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =1.4+1.2 \\\\  & =2.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-2)(y-2.6)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(1-2)(2-2.6)f(1,2) \\\\  & +(1-2)(4-2.6)f(1,4) \\\\  & +(3-2)(2-2.6)f(3,2) \\\\  & +(3-2)(4-2.6)f(3,4) \\\\  & =(-1)(-0.6)(0.5) \\\\  & +(-1)(1.4)(0) \\\\  & +(1)(-0.6)(0.2) \\\\  & +(1)(1.4)(0.3) \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
