    "q-146149": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146149",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=20,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=2,$ and $\\text{E}[XY]=44.8$ for two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =44.8-20\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of $X$ and $Y$ is $4.8.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
